-- title:
--   Real span of the period vectors is all of ℂⁿ
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure, and assume $F$ is a function field in one variable in the sense that there is an $x \in F$ transcendental over $\mathbb{C}$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\mathbb{C}(x)$ generated by $x$. Assume `IsCurveOver ℂ F`, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ has a divisor (a finitely supported integer-valued function on the set of places, a place being a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$, distinct from $F$ and a principal ideal ring) whose value at each place $v$ is $\mathrm{ord}_v(f)$ and whose degree is $0$, each residue field is finite over $\mathbb{C}$, and $\Omega[F/\mathbb{C}]$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$; assume `HasCanonicalDivisor`, i.e. every nonzero $\omega \in \Omega[F/\mathbb{C}]$ likewise has a divisor with value $v.\mathrm{ordDifferential}\,\omega$ at each $v$. Assume the place set $\mathrm{Place}\,\mathbb{C}\,F$ carries a topology and charts with model $\mathbb{C}$ making it a compact, Hausdorff, connected analytic manifold, and assume the hypothesis `hF`: for every nonzero $f \in F$ and every place $v$, the function $z \mapsto \mathrm{evalAt}\big((\mathrm{extChartAt}\ v)^{-1}(z)\big)\,f$ is meromorphic at the chart image of $v$ with meromorphic order exactly $\mathrm{ord}_v(f)$. Let $b = (b_i)_{i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n}$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-basis of the submodule `regularDifferentials ℂ F` of those $\omega$ which at every place $v$ can be written $\omega = f \cdot v.\mathrm{dCoord}$ with $f$ in the valuation subring of $v$. Then the $\mathbb{R}$-linear span of `pathPeriodLattice` of $b$ — the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathbb{C}$ generated by the vectors $\big(\int_\gamma b_i\big)_i$ as $\gamma$ runs over all loops at all places, the integral being the increment of a primitive of $b_i$ along $\gamma$ — is the whole of $\mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the "real span" half of the assertion that the group of periods of a basis of holomorphic differentials on a compact Riemann surface of genus $n$ is a full lattice in $\mathbb{C}^n$; combined with a finite-generation statement it yields discreteness of the period group. It is cited by [`AlgebraicCurve.discreteTopology_pathPeriodLattice_and_span_eq_top`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.discreteTopology_pathPeriodLattice_and_span_eq_top), by the period reciprocity statement [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_loops_pathIntegral_reciprocity_raw`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_loops_pathIntegral_reciprocity_raw), and by the Abel–Jacobi step [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_regular_pathIntegral_sub_eq_of_abelJacobiDiv_mem_pathPeriodLattice`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_regular_pathIntegral_sub_eq_of_abelJacobiDiv_mem_pathPeriodLattice).
